# HOS long (7–9 min, 5 parts)

Full steps: `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/STUDIO_PLAYBOOK.md` §2–§4 and §7. Hooks: `HOS_STRATEGY.md` → *Long hook*.

- **Topic:** a familiar thing and the moment we found out the truth about it; one person, one room, one proof. No existing public long on that subject. Competition check on the exact title (signed out, top five). Fill `PRE_BUILD_VIDIQ_AUDIT.md`. **Ben picks.**
- **Script** (about 1,200–1,300 spoken words, real narration, not holds):
  - The first 3 s of picture are the story. Sentence one is the promise; the payoff is named by 30 s.
  - First minute (26 Sep 2026): answer image by 0:05, title question spoken by 0:08, promise by 0:15, stakes by 0:25, first real fact before 0:45, picture change every 4–6 s, no intro or title card, part 01 has no chapter card.
  - 5 acts, cause and effect. Clear before clever: name the thing, say what it is and why it mattered in the same breath, one idea at a time. Always say what the discovery made possible.
  - The Explorer in 1–3 beats only, never in the first minute (a faceless hand if needed). Every claim sourced. No goodbye and no subscribe ask; the last line hands off to the next film.
  - At least two "you" moments. Facts right for the year in the scene ("we now know…" for modern values); honest rounding; quotes attributed.
  - End: last line → 3–4 s cream end card → 20 s Studio end screen. No on-screen "SEE <film>" labels.
  - File format: spoken prose plus markers only (labels inside `[VISUAL MUST: … · LABEL: …]`); no VO in tables; notes, fact notes, launch plan and change log in the film's README, `FACT_NOTES_vNN.md` and `11_Upload-Package/LAUNCH_PLAN.md`; one live `*_master_*` file, older versions renamed without "master".
  - Write a main title + one Test & Compare alternative and a launch plan in the HOS_STRATEGY week alongside the script. Part times are estimates; re-time from the recorded VO.
  - Quote the reviewer score as it is; never pad or edit the reviewer to pass a script.
  - `[CHAPTER CARD]`, `[VISUAL MUST]` and `[TEACH]` on every act; `[EXPLORER ACTS]` on Explorer beats only.
- **Gates:** `npm run review:script` scores 90 or more, then `npm run gate:episode` PASSes. No VO or picture spend before both.
- **Voice:** Ben Orbit Narrator (`04_Audio/tools/orbit_voice.py`, `settings_for_part(n)`: speed 1.04 on every part; `eleven_v3` ignores higher speeds). VO before picture; the text is locked (regenerate a single sentence, never rewrite). Target full VO about 8:15–8:30. Run `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/tools/vo_check.py` on every take (word diff, loudness −19 to −28 dB, pauses, pace, first-minute times) before Ben listens. Too long: trim pauses to ~0.6 s, then `atempo` ≤ 1.06. Record part durations, starts and sha256 in `production-status.md`, then re-time from the real VO.
- **Title for traction:** the question the film answers, phrased as searched, least big-channel competition (`tools/public_search.py`); umbrella and picture-led titles go into Test & Compare. vidIQ may be waived by Ben; gate overrides are Ben's alone and are recorded in the audit and status.
- **Assembly:**
  - normalise to 1920×1080, 30 fps CFR, stereo; check A/V lengths match;
  - a remint is picture only (keep the locked audio);
  - no branded intro; soft chapter cards; bed about −20 dB under VO;
  - out on the 3–4 s cream-on-brown card *History of Science / DISCOVERY. WONDER. PROOF.*; subscribe in the Studio end screen only;
  - export `09_Final-Export/<slug>_full_v0N.mp4`.
- **Publish:** normal publish, Thursday 18:00 UK, no Premiere. Test & Compare with 3 thumbs; end screen = best related long + Subscribe; captions from the script; a pinned comment with the film's open question.
- Keep `production-status.md` current on `main`.
